.TH FBSET 1 "June 12, 2026"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
fbset \- show or select the N64 framebuffer mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbset
[
.I 320x240
|
.I 640x480
]
.PP
.B fbset
[
.I width height
]
.PP
.B fbset
.B fill
.I rgba5551
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbset
queries or changes the active N64 framebuffer mode through
.IR /dev/fb0 .
The framebuffer is always 16-bit RGBA5551.
.PP
With no arguments,
.B fbset
prints the current mode, framebuffer address, active TV type, and detected
RDRAM size.
.PP
The
.B fill
form fills the current framebuffer with a 16-bit RGBA5551 value through the
fixed user framebuffer mapping returned by
.IR /dev/fb0 .
This is a direct mapping smoke test, not a write(2) transfer.
.PP
The 320x240 mode is available on all supported N64 memory configurations.
The 640x480 mode requires an Expansion Pak and returns an error on a 4 MiB
system.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the current framebuffer mode:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fbset
.fi
.RE
.PP
Switch to 640x480 on an 8 MiB system:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fbset 640x480
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fill the screen through the user framebuffer mapping:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fbset fill 0x001f
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP 12
.I /dev/fb0
N64 framebuffer device
